  (145,001,199 bytes, SHA-256 3043896e25fead6114f29bf85be987104abb2865db9f816edff0562b1c31820d)

Kept: of the file's 311,600 rows (5,003 storms), each storm's main
track (the 11,161 rows of spur tracks, alternative positions kept for storms
that merged or split, left out), for the 4,789 storms whose first point
falls from 1980 to 2025 (the newest season, still provisional, left out).
Of each point: the storm's id, name, season, the basin the point lies in,
the time (UTC), the one-minute sustained wind of the US agencies
(USA_WIND, knots), the Saffir-Simpson category IBTrACS derives from it
(USA_SSHS), and the distance to land. Longitudes that IBTrACS keeps
continuous past 180° (7,365 points) are brought back into -180 to 180.
Positions rounded to 0.01°. The points include the archive's 3-hourly
interpolated positions. The map's SQL joins each storm's points into
stretches of one category and splits a track where it crosses the
antimeridian, at the latitude where the step crosses.


